#, no-wrap
msgid "Create and normal-order the Hamiltonian {#create-and-normal-order-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Buat Hamiltonian dan lakukan normal-ordering {#create-and-normal-order-the-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the FCIDump data into a fermionic operator and applies normal ordering to simplify the operator structure.\n"
msgstr "Mengonversi data FCIDump menjadi operator fermionik dan menerapkan normal ordering untuk menyederhanakan struktur operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group terms by electronic structure {#group-terms-by-electronic-structure}"
msgstr "Kelompokkan suku berdasarkan struktur elektronik {#group-terms-by-electronic-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Groups related Hamiltonian terms by electronic structure before constructing their evolution circuits.\n"
msgstr "Mengelompokkan suku-suku Hamiltonian yang terkait berdasarkan struktur elektronik sebelum membangun circuit evolusinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate sampling weights, then normalize and map to qubit operators {#calculate-sampling-weights-then-normalize-and-map-to-qubit-operators}"
msgstr "Hitung bobot sampling, lalu normalisasi dan petakan ke operator qubit {#calculate-sampling-weights-then-normalize-and-map-to-qubit-operators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Order matters here.** Normalization rescales every coefficient to unit magnitude *in place*, so the sampling weights must be computed first. If normalization runs first, every $|c_j|$ reads back as exactly `1.0` and each group's weight collapses into a bare count of its terms — the sampling distribution would then be driven by group size rather than by the physical coefficients.\n"
msgstr "**Urutan penting di sini.** Normalisasi menskalakan ulang setiap koefisien menjadi magnitudo satu *di tempat*, sehingga bobot sampling harus dihitung lebih dulu. Kalau normalisasi dijalankan duluan, setiap $|c_j|$ terbaca persis `1.0` dan bobot tiap grup runtuh menjadi sekadar hitungan jumlah sukunya — distribusi sampling lalu akan ditentukan oleh ukuran grup, bukan oleh koefisien fisiknya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each group's weight is the **mean** absolute coefficient of its terms. The Python tab's `QDriftTrotterization` pass uses the same weight for a grouped Hamiltonian. Using the sum instead would make $\\lambda$ scale with group size, which in turn skews the evolution time $t_k = \\lambda\\tau/n$.\n"
msgstr "Bobot tiap grup adalah koefisien absolut **rata-rata** dari suku-sukunya. Pass `QDriftTrotterization` di tab Python memakai bobot yang sama untuk Hamiltonian yang dikelompokkan. Kalau memakai jumlah, $\\lambda$ akan ikut membesar seiring ukuran grup, yang pada gilirannya membuat waktu evolusi $t_k = \\lambda\\tau/n$ condong.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The weight $\\lambda_i = \\frac{1}{|G_i|}\\sum_{j \\in G_i} |c_{ij}|$ is the mean absolute coefficient over the terms of group $G_i$, read from the original coefficients. Normalization then rescales each fermionic term to unit magnitude before the Jordan-Wigner transformation, preserving only its phase/sign in the evolved operator. This matches qDRIFT's normalized-term evolution: coefficient magnitudes determine sampling probabilities via $\\lambda$, while the circuit evolution uses the normalized term so large coefficients are not counted twice.\n"
msgstr "Bobot $\\lambda_i = \\frac{1}{|G_i|}\\sum_{j \\in G_i} |c_{ij}|$ adalah koefisien absolut rata-rata atas suku-suku grup $G_i$, dibaca dari koefisien aslinya. Normalisasi kemudian menskalakan ulang tiap suku fermionik menjadi magnitudo satu sebelum transformasi Jordan-Wigner, sehingga hanya fase/tandanya yang tersisa pada operator yang dievolusikan. Ini sesuai dengan evolusi suku ternormalisasi pada qDRIFT: magnitudo koefisien menentukan probabilitas sampling lewat $\\lambda$, sedangkan evolusi circuit memakai suku yang sudah dinormalisasi sehingga koefisien besar tidak dihitung dua kali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample operator sets {#sample-operator-sets}"
msgstr "Sampling set operator {#sample-operator-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Draws the operator sets for 100 random circuits, each containing 10 groups sampled from the weighted distribution. The next step turns these sets into the ensemble of qDRIFT circuits.\n"
msgstr "Mengambil set operator untuk 100 circuit acak, masing-masing berisi 10 grup yang disampel dari distribusi berbobot. Langkah berikutnya mengubah set-set ini menjadi ensemble circuit qDRIFT.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Build the qDRIFT circuits (C++) {#step-2-build-the-qdrift-circuits-c}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Bangun circuit qDRIFT (C++) {#step-2-build-the-qdrift-circuits-c}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the C++ version, this step builds the circuits from the sampled operator sets. Transpilation for the target backend happens in Step 3, immediately before each circuit is submitted.\n"
msgstr "Pada versi C++, langkah ini membangun circuit dari set operator yang disampel. Transpilasi untuk backend target terjadi di Langkah 3, tepat sebelum tiap circuit dikirim.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The complete program then prints circuit statistics and the operator indices of circuit 0, which are omitted here.\n"
msgstr "Program lengkap kemudian mencetak statistik circuit dan indeks operator dari circuit 0, yang dihilangkan di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each sampled operator, creates a Suzuki-Trotter evolution circuit with time $t_k = \\frac{\\lambda \\tau}{n}$, where $n$ is the number of operators sampled per circuit and $\\tau$ is the time step. Because each sampled group was normalized term-by-term before mapping, this evolution applies only the phase/sign of each term during the rotation; the magnitudes contribute through the sampling distribution only. The Hartree-Fock initial state is prepared by applying X gates to qubits 0-6 and 10-16 (seven electrons in each spin sector). Each evolution circuit's instructions are manually appended to the main circuit using the C++ API.\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap operator yang disampel, dibuat circuit evolusi Suzuki-Trotter dengan waktu $t_k = \\frac{\\lambda \\tau}{n}$, di mana $n$ adalah jumlah operator yang disampel per circuit dan $\\tau$ adalah langkah waktu. Karena setiap grup yang disampel dinormalisasi suku demi suku sebelum pemetaan, evolusi ini hanya menerapkan fase/tanda dari tiap suku selama rotasi; magnitudonya berkontribusi hanya lewat distribusi sampling. State awal Hartree-Fock disiapkan dengan menerapkan gate X pada qubit 0-6 dan 10-16 (tujuh elektron di setiap sektor spin). Instruksi tiap circuit evolusi ditambahkan secara manual ke circuit utama memakai API C++.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives (C++) {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-c}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan primitif Qiskit (C++) {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-c}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connects to IBM Quantum, selects the backend by name, transpiles each circuit for that backend, and submits **one job per circuit**: 100 separate Sampler jobs of 100 shots each on a 20-qubit register. It then polls each job until it finishes and collects the bitstrings from `result[0]`. Every job uses QPU time and waits in the queue separately, so expect this step to take much longer than a single batched job.\n"
msgstr "Terhubung ke IBM Quantum, memilih backend berdasarkan nama, men-transpile tiap circuit untuk backend itu, dan mengirim **satu job per circuit**: 100 job Sampler terpisah masing-masing 100 shot pada register 20 qubit. Lalu ia mem-polling tiap job sampai selesai dan mengumpulkan bitstring dari `result[0]`. Setiap job memakai waktu QPU dan mengantre sendiri-sendiri, jadi langkah ini akan memakan waktu jauh lebih lama daripada satu job batch.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The hardware results quoted on this page come from a run on `ibm_pittsburgh` (100 circuits × 100 shots), with `backend_name` changed from the default `ibm_fez`. The saved samples were postprocessed with the corrected determinant bit ordering shown in Step 4. Hardware noise varies between runs, so your counts and final energy will differ.\n"
msgstr "Hasil hardware yang dikutip di halaman ini berasal dari eksekusi di `ibm_pittsburgh` (100 circuit × 100 shot), dengan `backend_name` diubah dari default `ibm_fez`. Sampel yang tersimpan diproses ulang dengan urutan bit determinan yang sudah dikoreksi seperti ditunjukkan di Langkah 4. Noise hardware bervariasi antar eksekusi, jadi hitungan dan energi akhir kamu akan berbeda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Changing the backend:** Change `backend_name` in `SqDRIFT.cpp` to target a different device; `service.backends()` lists what your account can reach.\n"
msgstr "**Mengganti backend:** Ubah `backend_name` di `SqDRIFT.cpp` untuk menargetkan perangkat lain; `service.backends()` menampilkan daftar yang bisa dijangkau akunmu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format (C++) {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format-c}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Post-process dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang diinginkan (C++) {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format-c}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Postselect bitstrings and write CI strings {#postselect-bitstrings-and-write-ci-strings}"
msgstr "Postseleksi bitstring dan tulis string CI {#postselect-bitstrings-and-write-ci-strings}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Postselects bitstrings with the correct Hamming weight (n_alpha spin-up, n_beta spin-down electrons, derived from the FCIDump `NELEC` field), converts them to Configuration Interaction (CI) strings using spin symmetrization, and writes them to `alphadets_from_sqd.txt` for subsequent Selected Basis Diagonalization.\n"
msgstr "Mempostseleksi bitstring dengan Hamming weight yang benar (n_alpha elektron spin-up, n_beta elektron spin-down, diturunkan dari field `NELEC` pada FCIDump), mengonversinya menjadi string Configuration Interaction (CI) memakai simetrisasi spin, dan menuliskannya ke `alphadets_from_sqd.txt` untuk Selected Basis Diagonalization berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clean up resources {#clean-up-resources}"
msgstr "Bersihkan resource {#clean-up-resources}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
