msgid "How this differs from the Python example {#how-this-differs-from-the-python-example}"
msgstr "Apa bedanya dengan contoh Python {#how-this-differs-from-the-python-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two examples differ in several respects at once, not only in how they treat bad-symmetry bitstrings, so they are not expected to produce identical energies:\n"
msgstr "Kedua contoh berbeda dalam beberapa hal sekaligus, bukan hanya cara menangani bitstring dengan simetri yang salah, jadi keduanya tidak diharapkan menghasilkan energi yang identik:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| | C++ tab | Python tab |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Bad-symmetry bitstrings | **Discarded** by `postselect_bitstrings` on Hamming weight | **Repaired** by iterative configuration recovery |\n"
"| Loop structure | Single pass: sample → postselect → diagonalize once | Outer loop: diagonalize, read orbital occupancies, recover configurations, re-diagonalize |\n"
"| Circuit count | 100 circuits (`num_circuits = 100`) | 400 circuits (200 per evolution time) |\n"
"| Evolution times | A single $\\tau$ (`time_step = 1`) | Two times, `times = [1.0, 10.0]` |\n"
"| Diagonal terms | Kept in the sampled operator | Removed by `filter_diagonal_terms`, changing the sampling distribution and the circuits |\n"
"| Term ordering | Grouped only | `canonical_order` applied before grouping for reproducibility |\n"
"| Diagonalization solver | **SBD** (`diag`, external MPI/OpenMP binary) | `qiskit-addon-sqd` in-process solver |\n"
"| Backend | Fixed by name (`backend_name = \"ibm_fez\"`; the run on this page used `ibm_pittsburgh`) | `least_busy` operational backend with enough qubits |\n"
"| Transpilation | Each circuit separately, optimization level 2 | All circuits together, optimization level 3 |\n"
"| Job submission | 100 jobs, one circuit each | One Sampler job containing all 400 circuits |\n"
"| Simulator run | None; hardware only | Noiseless simulator example before the hardware run |\n"
msgstr ""
"| | Tab C++ | Tab Python |\n"
"|---|---|---|\n"
"| Bitstring dengan simetri salah | **Dibuang** oleh `postselect_bitstrings` berdasarkan Hamming weight | **Diperbaiki** oleh pemulihan konfigurasi iteratif |\n"
"| Struktur loop | Sekali jalan: sampling → postseleksi → diagonalisasi sekali | Loop luar: diagonalisasi, baca okupansi orbital, pulihkan konfigurasi, diagonalisasi ulang |\n"
"| Jumlah circuit | 100 circuit (`num_circuits = 100`) | 400 circuit (200 per waktu evolusi) |\n"
"| Waktu evolusi | Satu $\\tau$ saja (`time_step = 1`) | Dua waktu, `times = [1.0, 10.0]` |\n"
"| Suku diagonal | Dipertahankan di operator yang disampel | Dihapus oleh `filter_diagonal_terms`, mengubah distribusi sampling dan circuit |\n"
"| Pengurutan suku | Hanya dikelompokkan | `canonical_order` diterapkan sebelum pengelompokan demi reproduksibilitas |\n"
"| Solver diagonalisasi | **SBD** (`diag`, binary MPI/OpenMP eksternal) | Solver in-process `qiskit-addon-sqd` |\n"
"| Backend | Tetap berdasarkan nama (`backend_name = \"ibm_fez\"`; eksekusi di halaman ini memakai `ibm_pittsburgh`) | Backend operasional `least_busy` dengan qubit yang cukup |\n"
"| Transpilasi | Tiap circuit terpisah, optimization level 2 | Semua circuit sekaligus, optimization level 3 |\n"
"| Pengiriman job | 100 job, satu circuit per job | Satu job Sampler berisi semua 400 circuit |\n"
"| Eksekusi simulator | Tidak ada; hanya hardware | Contoh simulator noiseless sebelum eksekusi hardware |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both versions use the same Hamiltonian, group its terms by electronic structure, weight each group by the mean absolute coefficient of its terms, start from the Hartree-Fock state, and sample 10 groups and 100 shots per circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kedua versi memakai Hamiltonian yang sama, mengelompokkan sukunya berdasarkan struktur elektronik, membobot tiap grup dengan koefisien absolut rata-rata dari sukunya, mulai dari state Hartree-Fock, dan men-sampling 10 grup serta 100 shot per circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each difference affects the sampled subspace, and therefore the energy, independently. The larger ensemble and the second, longer evolution time both broaden the configurations the Python example explores; sampling at more than one time gives SqDRIFT its Krylov-like coverage of the low-energy space. Filtering diagonal terms changes which operators the sampler can draw and their weights, so the two runs sample different distributions.\n"
msgstr "Tiap perbedaan memengaruhi subruang yang disampel, dan karena itu energinya, secara independen. Ensemble yang lebih besar dan waktu evolusi kedua yang lebih panjang sama-sama memperluas konfigurasi yang dijelajahi contoh Python; sampling pada lebih dari satu waktu memberi SqDRIFT cakupan ala Krylov atas ruang energi rendah. Memfilter suku diagonal mengubah operator mana yang bisa diambil sampler beserta bobotnya, jadi kedua eksekusi men-sampling distribusi yang berbeda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Postselection is a strict filter, and a shot with the wrong particle number is dropped outright. In the run above that discarded most of the data, 1137 of 10000 shots survived the (7,7) Hamming-weight check (about 11%), collapsing into just 49 distinct $\\alpha$-determinants. Configuration recovery instead uses average orbital occupancies from a prior diagonalization to flip bits and *repair* such shots, recycling what postselection would discard. That feedback makes it inherently iterative: `recover_configurations` in `qiskit-addon-sqd-hpc` requires an `avg_occupancies` argument that exists only after a diagonalization has run.\n"
msgstr "Postseleksi adalah filter yang ketat, dan shot dengan jumlah partikel yang salah langsung dibuang. Pada eksekusi di atas, itu membuang sebagian besar data: 1137 dari 10000 shot lolos pengecekan Hamming-weight (7,7) (sekitar 11%), yang menciut menjadi hanya 49 $\\alpha$-determinan yang berbeda. Sebaliknya, pemulihan konfigurasi memakai okupansi orbital rata-rata dari diagonalisasi sebelumnya untuk membalik bit dan *memperbaiki* shot semacam itu, mendaur ulang apa yang akan dibuang postseleksi. Umpan balik itu membuatnya inheren iteratif: `recover_configurations` di `qiskit-addon-sqd-hpc` membutuhkan argumen `avg_occupancies` yang baru ada setelah diagonalisasi dijalankan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This C++ run yields a subspace of 49 $\\alpha$-determinants and an energy of `-107.5109` Ha. The full $\\alpha$-determinant space for seven electrons in 10 orbitals is only $\\binom{10}{7} = 120$ strings, so feeding all 120 to the same `diag` binary gives the exact FCI energy `-107.6482` Ha. The run therefore sits about `0.1373` Ha above exact while spanning 49 of the 120 $\\alpha$-determinants. Since SQD is variational in the selected subspace, a smaller subspace can only raise the energy, so the incomplete subspace is the most direct reading of the gap.\n"
msgstr "Eksekusi C++ ini menghasilkan subruang berisi 49 $\\alpha$-determinan dan energi `-107.5109` Ha. Ruang $\\alpha$-determinan penuh untuk tujuh elektron di 10 orbital hanya $\\binom{10}{7} = 120$ string, jadi memasukkan semua 120 ke binary `diag` yang sama menghasilkan energi FCI eksak `-107.6482` Ha. Jadi eksekusi ini berada sekitar `0.1373` Ha di atas nilai eksak sambil mencakup 49 dari 120 $\\alpha$-determinan. Karena SQD bersifat variasional dalam subruang terpilih, subruang yang lebih kecil hanya bisa menaikkan energi, sehingga subruang yang tidak lengkap adalah penjelasan paling langsung untuk selisih ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This exact-FCI check is only possible because the example is small; it is not part of the SqDRIFT workflow, and for system sizes where SQD is actually needed, no such reference exists. It serves here only to quantify how much of the space this run recovered.\n"
msgstr "Pengecekan FCI eksak ini hanya mungkin karena contohnya kecil; ini bukan bagian dari workflow SqDRIFT, dan untuk ukuran sistem yang benar-benar membutuhkan SQD, referensi seperti itu tidak ada. Di sini ia hanya berfungsi untuk mengukur seberapa banyak ruang yang berhasil dipulihkan eksekusi ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A comparison against the Python example is not controlled, so a difference should not be attributed to the absence of configuration recovery alone; note that circuit count, the single evolution time, diagonal-term filtering, and hardware noise all differ at once and all shape the subspace.\n"
msgstr "Perbandingan dengan contoh Python tidak terkontrol, jadi perbedaan tidak boleh dikaitkan hanya dengan tidak adanya pemulihan konfigurasi; perhatikan bahwa jumlah circuit, waktu evolusi tunggal, penyaringan suku diagonal, dan noise hardware semuanya berbeda sekaligus dan semuanya membentuk subruang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To close the gap, here are some possible next steps to try after completing this tutorial: raise `shots`, `num_circuits`, or `ops_per_circuit`; sample at more than one `time_step`; and add a recovery loop on top of `Qiskit::addon::sqd::recover_configurations`.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menutup selisih itu, berikut beberapa langkah lanjutan yang bisa dicoba setelah menyelesaikan tutorial ini: naikkan `shots`, `num_circuits`, atau `ops_per_circuit`; lakukan sampling pada lebih dari satu `time_step`; dan tambahkan loop pemulihan di atas `Qiskit::addon::sqd::recover_configurations`.\n"

